===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/æbˈsti.mi.əs.nəs/|/əbˈsti.mi.əs.nəs/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-abstemiousness.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The quality of being [[abstemious]], [[temperate]], or [[sparing]], particularly in the use of food and strong drinks. {{defdate|from early 17th c.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=9}}</ref>
#* {{RQ:Lamb Essays of Elia|version=Last|page=ix|passage=He was temperate in his meals and diversions, but always kept a little on this side of '''abstemiousness'''. Only in the use of the Indian weed he might be thought a little excessive.}}

====Usage notes====
* It expresses a greater degree of [[abstinence]] than {{m|en|temperance}}.

